  "notes": [
    "The downstream app keeps its routing, user/session model, and SDK client shape; only the cliUrl points to the adapter.",
    "The adapter owns translation: SDK session/create/resume/send becomes Codex thread/start/resume/turn, while tools, approvals, sandbox, and protocol-version routing are mapped at the boundary.",
    "Session continuity is explicit: the runtime store binds SDK session ids to Codex thread ids plus cwd and tool fingerprint, so incompatible resume fails early.",
    "Proof is read-back, not narration: the harness checks logs, adapter transcript, SQLite side effects, tool intent, schema round-trip, and pass/fail/not-run artifacts."
  ]
